╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

================================================================
  Network tree
================================================================

[network] Global Network/
  [region] West Region/
    [airport] LAX  (cap: 4, routes: 3)
    [airport] SFO  (cap: 3, routes: 2)
  [region] East Region/
    [airport] JFK  (cap: 5, routes: 4)
    [airport] ORD  (cap: 3, routes: 2)

================================================================
  Client queries — same call regardless of node type
================================================================

  Global Network   get_capacity()=15   get_route_count()=11
  West Region      get_capacity()= 7   get_route_count()=5
  East Region      get_capacity()= 8   get_route_count()=6
  LAX (leaf)       get_capacity()= 4   get_route_count()=3
  JFK (leaf)       get_capacity()= 5   get_route_count()=4

================================================================
  Without Composite
================================================================

  Every caller would need:
    if isinstance(node, Airport):        return node.capacity
    if isinstance(node, RegionalNetwork): loop airports
    if isinstance(node, AirportNetwork):  loop regions + loop airports
    if new level added:                   add another branch...

  With Composite:
    node.get_capacity()  — works at every level, always

